---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
const updated = '2026-08-17';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="Terms of use for the Brandure website, covering site content, research accuracy, data handling and enquiries."
>
  <h1>Terms</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Terms of use for this website. Last updated
    <time datetime={updated}>17 August 2026</time>.
  </p>

  <p class="note">
    Placeholder. These terms cover use of the website only. They are not legal
    advice, have not been reviewed by a lawyer, and do not cover client
    engagements — those are governed by a separate written agreement. Replace
    before launch.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This site is operated by {SITE.legalName}. Contact:
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Use of this site</h2>
  <p>
    You may read, quote and link to material published here with attribution.
    You may not republish substantial extracts as your own work, or present our
    research as having been produced by someone else.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Research and accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    Research published here describes what specific AI answer engines returned
    for specific prompts, at the time stated. Answer engines change. Findings
    are a point-in-time record and are not a forecast of what any engine will
    return in future, nor a guarantee of results from any engagement.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a method has known limits — sample size, session state, model tier —
    those are stated in the piece itself. Read them before relying on a figure.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Enquiries and downloads</h2>
  <p>
    If you submit a form, we use your details to reply and to send the material
    requested. We do not sell them. Ask us to delete them and we will.
  </p>

  <h2>5. No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    This site is provided as-is. We make no warranty that it will be
    uninterrupted or error-free, and we are not liable for decisions taken on
    the basis of published material without independent verification.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Governing law</h2>
  <p>Placeholder — jurisdiction to be confirmed.</p>
</BaseLayout>
